    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247-a2">

                <pb facs="0529" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg459"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Citizen, No</hi>. 162 <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Salle
                                Street, &amp;c.</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chicago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1883-09-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 25,
                    1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The undersigned were appointed a
                    committee to wait on you and present the following resolution passed at a large
                    and influential meeting of Irish-American citizens in this city:</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That P. W. Dunne, J. F. Scanlan, D. F.
                    Gleeson, D. O’Sullivan, and T. P. O’Conner be appointed a committee to wait upon
                    Hon. J. F. Finerty to request <pb facs="0530" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/> him to
                    communicate with the Secretary of State to ascertain what measures, if any, the
                    Government of the United States is disposed to take to have O’Donnell, as an
                    American citizen, properly defended at his forthcoming trial for the alleged
                    killing of the informer Carey, and to urge upon the Secretary of State the
                    necessity for immediate action by the United States Government to vindicate the
                    right of citizen O’Donnell to a fair trial, as provided for under international
                    law existing between this country and Great Britain.”</p>
                <p>Soliciting your prompt attention,</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>P. W. DUNNE.</item>
                            <item>DAN. O’SULLIVAN.</item>
                            <item>T. P. O’CONNER.</item>
                            <item>JNO. F. SCANLAN.</item>
                            <item>D. F. GLEESON.</item>
                            <item>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">John F. Finerty.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
